{"abstract":"Background: Preventive health checks are assumed to reduce the risk of the development of cardio-metabolic disease in the long term. Although no solid evidence of effect is shown on health checks targeting the general population, studies suggest positive effects if health checks target people or groups identified at risk of disease. The aim of this study is to explore why and how targeted preventive health checks work, for whom they work, and under which circumstances they can be expected to work. Methods: The study is designed as a realist synthesis that consists of four phases, each including collection and analysis of empirical data: 1) Literature search of systematic reviews and meta-analysis, 2) Interviews with key-stakeholders, 3) Literature search of qualitative studies and grey literature, and 4) Workshops with key stakeholders and end-users. Through the iterative analysis we identified the interrelationship between contexts, mechanisms, and outcomes to develop a program theory encompassing hypotheses about targeted preventive health checks. Results: Based on an iterative analysis of the data material, we developed a final program theory consisting of seven themes; Target group; Recruitment and participation; The encounter between professional and participants; Follow-up activities; Implementation and operation; Shared understanding of the intervention; and Unintended side effects. Overall, the data material showed that targeted preventive health checks need to be accessible, recognizable, and relevant for the participants’ everyday lives as well as meaningful to the professionals involved. The results showed that identifying a target group, that both benefit from attending and have the resources to participate pose a challenge for targeted preventive health check interventions. This challenge illustrates the importance of designing the recruitment and intervention activities according to the target groups particular life situation. Conclusion: The results indicate that a one-size-fits-all model of targeted preventive health checks should be abandoned, and that intervention activities and implementation depend on for whom and under which circumstances the intervention is initiated. Based on the results we suggest that future initiatives conduct thorough needs assessment as the basis for decisions about where and how the preventive health checks are implemented.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Nanna Bjørnbak","Nilou, Freja Ekstrøm","Thilsing, Trine","Larsen, Lars Bruun","Østergaard, Jane Nautrup","Broholm-Jørgensen, Marie"],"cuid":["S02-099.94-704090"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Broholm-Jørgensen, Marie"],"keyword":["Chronic Disease","Denmark","Humans","Intervention research","Participatory research","Preventive Health Services","Preventive health checks","Qualitative Research","Realist synthesis","Systematic Reviews as Topic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring targeted preventive health check interventions a realist synthesis","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-023-16861-8","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["LBL og JNO are employed at Steno Diabetes Center Zealand and Aarhus respectively, research institutions partly funded by unrestricted grants from Novo Nordisk Foundation. Open access funding provided by University Library of Southern Denmark This study was funded by a collaboration between Steno Diabetes Centre Zealand, Steno Diabetes Centre Odense, Steno Diabetes Centre Aarhus, Steno Diabetes Centre Nord and the Region of Southern Denmark. The authors would like to thank all the study participants for sharing their valuable experiences. Furthermore, we would like to send a special thanks to the steering committee of this study; Lars Bruun Larsen (LBL), Jane Nautrup Østergaard (JNØ), Magnus Falby (MF), Marianne Gellert Krogh (MGK), Tina Heide (TH) and Arne Gårn (AG) for their involvement in, and valuable contributions to the entire research process. We would also like to thank Anders Larrabee Sønderlund for thorough proofreading of the manuscript."],"id":"S02-099.94-704090","identifier":[{"id":"85173765108","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10557298","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37798691","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-45ac4621-1e46-4bb2-b1d9-03ef16d7e5ed","sdu-14175acf-0106-4e70-9541-ff6e34895607"],"keyword":["Chronic disease","Denmark","Humans","Intervention research","Participatory research","Preventive Health Services","Preventive health checks","Qualitative Research","Realist synthesis","Systematic Reviews as Topic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-94037F013BB8CB3D8CF7E744CC39AF50"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-023-16861-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/245581636/s12889_023_16861_8.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health, Social health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Center Sjælland"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - SDCA-Steno Diabetes Center Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna Bjørnbak","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"c5494300-cce7-4e1c-9e68-4db844ff8f25","name":"Christoffersen, Nanna Bjørnbak","orcid":"0009-0007-8512-5150","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Freja Ekstrøm","key":"niloupau","last":"Nilou","locid":"a716858d-2be3-42a7-93b7-c5a6725a2cca","name":"Nilou, Freja","name_org":"Nilou, Freja Ekstrøm","orcid":"0009-0001-6108-4055","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"thilsingpau","last":"Thilsing","locid":"6ae25242-1e96-48cf-ab01-cbac26690f6b","name":"Thilsing, Trine","orcid":"0000-0002-2041-2219","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Bruun","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"1418e278-0f71-406e-b479-3429aca4b01d","name":"Bruun Larsen, Lars","name_org":"Larsen, Lars Bruun","orcid":"0000-0001-9120-4751","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jane Nautrup","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"b8584d68-9cc9-4cf7-ada6-d882ca76e987","name":"Østergaard, Jane Nautrup","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"broholmjørgensenpau","last":"Broholm-Jørgensen","locid":"d708f0b7-bad5-4faa-b5a2-900ea6bf97bd","name":"Broholm-Jørgensen, Marie","orcid":"0000-0001-9005-0754","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37798691"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12889-023-16861-8","issn":["14712458"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Public Health","paperid":"1928","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Public Health","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173765108"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-45ac4621-1e46-4bb2-b1d9-03ef16d7e5ed","sdu-14175acf-0106-4e70-9541-ff6e34895607"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Exploring targeted preventive health check interventions – a realist synthesis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.94-704090","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Psychotherapy is regarded as a highly efficient treatment across many different types of psychological disturbances. In most arenas of life, practice tends to improve performance considerably. Surprisingly, this does not generally seem to be the case for psychotherapists. For some reason, they do not appear to improve in terms of efficiency as time goes by - at least not unless they deliberately attempt to improve. To our knowledge, the effects of practice has not yet been studied in psychotherapists working with older clients. The current study intends to investigate the effects of practice on the outcome of psychotherapy for elderly persons. It will follow 4 psychologists for the first 2 years of their professional lives to explore whether increased practice leads to better outcomes for their clients. The clients consist primarily of elderly persons above the age of 65, who receives psychotherapy to improve their overall well-being and lower feelings of anxiety and depression. Regression analyses are planned with outcome improvement functioning as the dependent variable, calculated as pre-treatment scores subtracted from post-treatment scores. To account for individual differences in skill, the dependent variable is mean centered for each psychologist. The independent variable is the chronological rank for each client for each psychologist. As the investigated psychotherapists work within a deliberate therapeutic praxis, which utilizes systematic outcome monitoring, we expect to find a significant, but small, effect of practice on the outcome of treatment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Morten","Larsen, Lars","Vedel, Anna"],"cuid":["S02-092.11-822232"],"event":{"end":"2022-01-09","place":"Honolulu, us","start":"2022-01-06","title":"The IAFOR International Conference on Education in Hawaii 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does practice always make perfect do psychotherapists treating older adults become more efficient as they gain more experience","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/257366535/iice_programme_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-092.11-822232","ids":["aau-0b016487-6c73-4173-b389-b6cc7c696346","au-ad90125b-abd6-40ec-9766-d0701a9903cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-2E7448C4EA60880D09E15A3A78C90162"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/789966589/iice_programme_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/257366535/iice_programme_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Psychology of Culture, Humanity and Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"cc69f65a-9162-4ebe-8585-b2b3ac5f762d","name":"Christoffersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9423-4654","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7bd13f67-d81b-40d2-a742-8115e7100ecb","name":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1603-0311","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna","key":"pacakvedelpau","last":"Pacak-Vedel","locid":"717ee2a9-75d4-4f25-987d-96999aad6fee","name":"Vedel, Anna","name_org":"Pacak-Vedel, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-6789-8992","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0b016487-6c73-4173-b389-b6cc7c696346","au-ad90125b-abd6-40ec-9766-d0701a9903cb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Does practice always make perfect? : Do psychotherapists treating older adults become more efficient as they gain more experience","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.11-822232","year":2022,"yearsub":2022}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Lars","Vedel, Anna","Christoffersen, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-168061"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"livsløbsudviklingen af intelligens og dens sammenhæng med centrale livsudfald","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-168061","ids":["au-44038927-4f3d-48b8-ae52-fa39995185c8"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-BD84EAB5CA2900166FBB0AF067B56594"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7bd13f67-d81b-40d2-a742-8115e7100ecb","name":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1603-0311","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"pacakvedelpau","last":"Pacak-Vedel","locid":"717ee2a9-75d4-4f25-987d-96999aad6fee","name":"Vedel, Anna","name_org":"Pacak-Vedel, Anna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"cc69f65a-9162-4ebe-8585-b2b3ac5f762d","name":"Christoffersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9423-4654","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/pl.v43i2.137308","issn":["01071211"],"issue":"2","journal":"Psyke & Logos","pages":"158-185","publisher":"Dansk Psykologisk Forlag","status":"p","title":"Psyke & Logos","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-44038927-4f3d-48b8-ae52-fa39995185c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Livsløbsudviklingen af intelligens og dens sammenhæng med centrale livsudfald","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-168061","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Psychotherapy is regarded as a highly efficient treatment across many different types of psychological disturbances. In most arenas of life, practice tends to improve performance considerably. Surprisingly, this does not generally seem to be the case for psychotherapists. For some reason, they do not appear to improve in terms of efficiency as time goes by - at least not unless they deliberately attempt to improve. To our knowledge, the effects of practice has not yet been studied in psychotherapists working with older clients. The current study intends to investigate the effects of practice on the outcome of psychotherapy for elderly persons. It will follow 4 psychologists for the first 2 years of their professional lives to explore whether increased practice leads to better outcomes for their clients. The clients consist primarily of elderly persons above the age of 65, who receives psychotherapy to improve their overall well-being and lower feelings of anxiety and depression. Regression analyses are planned with outcome improvement functioning as the dependent variable, calculated as pre-treatment scores subtracted from post-treatment scores. To account for individual differences in skill, the dependent variable is mean centered for each psychologist. The independent variable is the chronological rank for each client for each psychologist. As the investigated psychotherapists work within a deliberate therapeutic praxis, which utilizes systematic outcome monitoring, we expect to find a significant, but small, effect of practice on the outcome of treatment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Morten","Larsen, Lars","Vedel, Anna"],"cuid":["S02-080.56-822407"],"event":{"end":"2022-01-09","place":"Honolulu, Hawaii, us","start":"2022-01-06","title":"The 7th IAFOR International Conference on Education in Hawaii","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does practice always make perfect a study of whether psychotherapists treating older adults become more efficient as they gain more experience","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/iice2022/IICE2022_61467.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-080.56-822407","ids":["aau-9cf95498-8cc0-4376-b393-8eac55263325","au-277a0a45-19f8-4102-bdaa-bd0c1d2c117a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9CC87E4D034B546A523C3CCBFCBE3888"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://papers.iafor.org/wp-content/uploads/papers/iice2022/IICE2022_61467.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Psychology of Culture, Humanity and Education"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"cc69f65a-9162-4ebe-8585-b2b3ac5f762d","name":"Christoffersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9423-4654","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7bd13f67-d81b-40d2-a742-8115e7100ecb","name":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1603-0311","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anna","key":"pacakvedelpau","last":"Pacak-Vedel","locid":"717ee2a9-75d4-4f25-987d-96999aad6fee","name":"Vedel, Anna","name_org":"Pacak-Vedel, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-6789-8992","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"2022","issn":["21891036"],"pages":"1-4","series":"The IAFOR International Conference on Education Proceedings","status":"p","title":"The IAFOR International Conference on Education – Hawaii 2022 Official Conference Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9cf95498-8cc0-4376-b393-8eac55263325","au-277a0a45-19f8-4102-bdaa-bd0c1d2c117a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Does practice always make perfect? A study of whether psychotherapists treating older adults become more efficient as they gain more experience","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-080.56-822407","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Fast surveillance strategies are needed to control the spread of new emerging SARS-CoV-2 variants and gain time for evaluation of their pathogenic potential. This was essential for the Omicron variant (B.1.1.529) that replaced the Delta variant (B.1.617.2) and is currently the dominant SARS-CoV-2 variant circulating worldwide. RT-qPCR strategies complement whole genome sequencing, especially in resource lean countries, but mutations in the targeting primer and probe sequences of new emerging variants can lead to a failure of the existing RT-qPCRs. Here, we introduced an RT-qPCR platform for detecting the Delta- and the Omicron variant simultaneously using a degenerate probe targeting the key ΔH69/V70 mutation in the spike protein. By inclusion of the L452R mutation into the RT-qPCR platform, we could detect not only the Delta and the Omicron variants, but also the Omicron sub-lineages BA.1, BA.2 and BA.4/BA.5. The RT-qPCR platform was validated in small- and large-scale. It can easily be incorporated for continued monitoring of Omicron sub-lineages, and offers a fast adaption strategy of existing RT-qPCRs to detect new emerging SARS-CoV-2 variants using degenerate probes.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Jessen, Randi","Nielsen, Line","Larsen, Nicolai Balle","Cohen, Arieh Sierra","Gunalan, Vithiagaran","Marving, Ellinor","Alfaro-Núñez, Alonzo","Polacek, Charlotta","Fomsgaard, Anders","Spiess, Katja","Andersen, Kasper Skytte","Andersen, Martin Hjorth","Berg, Amalie","Bielidt, Susanne R.","Mølvang Dall, Sebastian","Dvarionaite, Erika","Hove Hansen, Susan","Jørgensen, Vibeke Rudkjøbing","Kirkegaard, Rasmus Hansen","Saei, Wagma","Nicolajsen, Trine B.","Østergaard, Stine Karstenskov","Brøndum, Rasmus Froberg","Bøgsted, Martin","Hose, Katja","Sagi, Tomer","Pakanec, Miroslaw","Fuglsang-Damgaard, David","Mølvadgaard, Mette","Krarup, Henrik","Nielsen, Marc T.K.","Jensen, Thomas BN"],"cuid":["S03-085.71-703806"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corpau":["Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium","The Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium (DCGC)"],"corresponding_author":["Spiess, Katja"],"keyword":["COVID 19 diagnosis","Genome Viral genetics","Humans","SARS CoV 2 genetics","Spike Glycoprotein Coronavirus genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Ukendt"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a rt qpcr system using a degenerate probe for specific identification and differentiation of sars cov 000000000002 omicron b 000000000001 000000000001 000000000529 variants of concern","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0274889","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-085.71-703806","identifier":[{"id":"36197885","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9534396","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85139364519","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-b68bef13-89c6-46a1-894c-9511f42ce907","ku-314912c0-0dc1-4718-ad65-5afe08511712","sdu-6ecf7268-f7b8-43d8-88da-826dc8a7a82d"],"keyword":["COVID-19/diagnosis","Genome, Viral/genetics","Humans","SARS-CoV-2/genetics","Spike Glycoprotein, Coronavirus/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-4A1FCF9AC7C3F9699FBA96DFC99B73A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/555219224/Jessen_et_al_2022_A_RT-qPCR_system_using_a_degenerate_probe.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/jo