://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-085.71-703806","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The Old Man’s Well-Being in Municipal Elder Care Lars Larsen, Morten Christoffersen Aarhus University, Denmark Contrary to what is sometimes believed, being an old man does not in itself constitute a risk factor. Neither old age nor male gender causes low well-being. In fact, age is positively related to well-being, and the risk of having low levels of well-being is higher for the old woman than for the old man. The objective of the present study is to determine whether this is also the case for the old man who depends on elder care. As care recipients suffer from poor health and a loss of functions necessary for independent daily living and lacks the autonomy enjoyed earlier in life, we hypothesize that levels of well-being will be lower than normal. We report results from a study on the old man’s well-being in elder care, drawing upon data from a large representative sample comprising of more than 2,000 care recipients (both men and women). Furthermore, we examine a sample of 354 elderly care recipients (both men and women) being treated for very low levels of well-being by way of psychotherapy. Though old men who receive municipal care score considerably lower than old men who do not, old women in the same situation score even lower. Levels of well-being in elderly with psychological problems were very low to low, but men had higher well-being than women. Psychotherapy resulted in more than 20 percent points of improvement from very low to normal for both genders. Men started out, and ended, at higher levels of well-being than women, but in terms of relative improvement, no significant gender difference was found. The relatively low level of well-being in care recipients in general, and its causes, should be used as a starting point for different types of prophylactic initiatives and interventions. One such promising intervention is psychotherapy.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Larsen, Lars","Christoffersen, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-172497"],"event":{"end":"2022-07-08","place":"Ljubljana, si","start":"2022-07-05","title":"The 17th European Congress of Psychology","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the old man s well being in municipal elder care","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-172497","ids":["au-4bc18652-3b50-4069-84ca-c4c306bfc83b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-854D528665EE9F22734016CC4BE0C450"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7bd13f67-d81b-40d2-a742-8115e7100ecb","name":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1603-0311","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"cc69f65a-9162-4ebe-8585-b2b3ac5f762d","name":"Christoffersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9423-4654","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4bc18652-3b50-4069-84ca-c4c306bfc83b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The old man’s well-being in municipal elder care","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-172497","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"As the population of elderly people continues to rise, the healthcare sector is increasingly faced with the challenge of maintaining high levels of well-being for elderly people who experience discontentment. This feeling of uneasiness, can be related to a number of issues, such as loneliness, anxiety, depression – or felt as a more generalised subjective sense of lowered well-being. The task facing the public health care sector, is to provide a reliable and broad method, in which these various issues are addressed. The current study aims to examine the effects of a public health initiative in the municipalities of Aarhus and Copenhagen, in which psychotherapy provided by psychologists is used for elderly people who experiences lowered well-being. The clients are primarily above the age of 65 and are either reffered to the initiatives by health care workers, family members or by themselves, if they experience lowered well-being. To asses the effects of treatment, anxiety and depression is measured through the use of the Common Mental Disorder Questionnaire, loneliness with the Three-Item Loneliness Scale and well-being with the WHO-5 Well-Being Index. We expect to replicate previous research by finding a large significant effect of treatment on well-being followed by significant moderate effects on anxiety and depression, with lesser - albeit significant, effects on loneliness.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Morten","Frandsen, Luise Moustgaard","Larsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-265168"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-30","place":"Reykavik, is","start":"2022-06-28","title":"The 13th Nordic Public Health Conference","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Christoffersen, Morten"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of public health initiatives on the well being of elderly persons","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-265168","ids":["au-ee00b006-a190-440f-bcbc-db7d7c1eb6cd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8029697F9C79A14E7D2B56974F3269F0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Capitol Region of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"cc69f65a-9162-4ebe-8585-b2b3ac5f762d","name":"Christoffersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9423-4654","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Luise Moustgaard","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","name":"Frandsen, Luise Moustgaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7bd13f67-d81b-40d2-a742-8115e7100ecb","name":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1603-0311","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ee00b006-a190-440f-bcbc-db7d7c1eb6cd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The effects of public health initiatives on the well-being of elderly persons","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-265168","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: In early 2021, the SARS-CoV-2 lineage B.1.1.7 (Alpha variant) became dominant across large parts of the world. In Denmark, comprehensive and real-time test, contact-tracing, and sequencing efforts were applied to sustain epidemic control. Here, we use these data to investigate the transmissibility, introduction, and onward transmission of B.1.1.7 in Denmark. Methods: We analyzed a comprehensive set of 60,178 SARS-CoV-2 genomes generated from high-throughput sequencing by the Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium, representing 34% of all positive cases in the period 14 November 2020 to 7 February 2021. We calculated the transmissibility of B.1.1.7 relative to other lineages using Poisson regression. Including all 1976 high-quality B.1.1.7 genomes collected in the study period, we constructed a time-scaled phylogeny, which was coupled with detailed travel history and register data to outline the introduction and onward transmission of B.1.1.7 in Denmark. Results: In a period with unchanged restrictions, we estimated an increased B.1.1.7 transmissibility of 58% (95% CI: [56%, 60%]) relative to other lineages. Epidemiological and phylogenetic analyses revealed that 37% of B.1.1.7 cases were related to the initial introduction in November 2020. The relative number of cases directly linked to introductions varied between 10 and 50% throughout the study period. Conclusions: Our findings corroborate early estimates of increased transmissibility of B.1.1.7. Both substantial early expansion when B.1.1.7 was still unmonitored and continuous foreign introductions contributed considerably to case numbers. Finally, our study highlights the benefit of balanced travel restrictions and self-isolation procedures coupled with comprehensive surveillance efforts, to sustain epidemic control in the face of emerging variants.","author_count":94,"contributors":["Michaelsen, Thomas Yssing","Bennedbæk, Marc","Christiansen, Lasse E.","Jørgensen, Mia S.F.","Møller, Camilla H.","Sørensen, Emil Aarre","Knutsson, Simon","Brandt, Jakob","Nymann, Thomas","Chiche-Lapierre, Clarisse","Collados, Emilio Fuster","Sørensen, Trine","Petersen, Celine","Le, Vang","Sereika, Mantas","Hansen, Frederik Teilfeldt","Rasmussen, Morten","Fonager, Jannik","Karst, Søren M.","Marvig, Rasmus L.","Stegger, Marc","Sieber, Raphael N.","Skov, Robert","Legarth, Rebecca","Krause, Tyra G.","Fomsgaard, Anders","Andersen, Kasper Skytte","Andersen, Martin Hjorth","Berg, Amalie","Bielidt, Susanne R.","Mølvang Dall, Sebastian","Dvarionaite, Erika","Hove Hansen, Susan","Jørgensen, Vibeke Rudkjøbing","Kirkegaard, Rasmus Hansen","Saei, Wagma","Nicolajsen, Trine B.","Østergaard, Stine Karstenskov","Brøndum, Rasmus Froberg","Bøgsted, Martin","Hose, Katja","Sagi, Tomer","Pakanec, Miroslaw","Fuglsang-Damgaard, David","Mølvadgaard, Mette","Krarup, Henrik","Svarrer, Christina W.","Christiansen, Mette T.","Ingham, Anna C.","Johannesen, Thor B.","Basterrechea, Martín","Lilje, Berit","Ellegaard, Kirsten","Matusevicius, Povilas","Christoffersen, Lars B.","Tang, Man Hung E.","Ng, Kim L.","Edslev, Sofie M.","Baig, Sharmin","Larsen, Ole H.","Skipper, Kristian A.","Vang, Søren","Handberg, Kurt J.","Nielsen, Marc T.K.","Kobel, Carl M.","Andersen, Camilla","Tarpgaard, Irene H.","Ellermann-Eriksen, Svend","Castruita, José A.S.","Schneider, Uffe V.","Jacobsen, Nana G.","Andersen, Christian","Pedersen, Martin S.","Schønning, Kristian","Kirkby, Nikolai","Nielsen, Lene","Nilsson, Line L.","Friis, Martin B.","Sundelin, Thomas","Hansen, Thomas A.","Skov, Marianne N.","Sydenham, Thomas V.","Nielsen, Xiaohui C.","Schouw, Christian H.","Jensen, Anders","Marmolin, Ea S.","Coia, John E.","Andersen, Dorte T.","Albertsen, Mads"],"cuid":["S04-093.49-010787"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corpau":["Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium","The Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium (DCGC)"],"corresponding_author":["Albertsen, Mads"],"keyword":["COVID 19 epidemiology","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Phylogeny","SARS CoV 2 genetics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction and transmission of sars cov 000000000002 lineage b 000000000001 000000000001 000000000007 alpha variant in denmark","src":["aau","dtu","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-022-01045-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work would not have been possible without the Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium (DCGC); a full list of contributing consortium members can be found in Additional file 1. We gratefully acknowledge the Danish hospitals for local sequencing and data sharing. Thanks to all data contributors from outside Denmark, including the authors and their originating laboratories responsible for obtaining the specimens, as well as their submitting laboratories for generating the genetic sequence and metadata and sharing it via the GISAID Initiative. A full acknowledgement table is provided in Additional file 2. We would like to acknowledge the people at Data Integration and Analysis (DIAS), Statens Serum Institute, for managing and maintaining the national MiBa database which much of this work is based on. Thanks to the people at the Danish Patient Safety Authority for providing us with detailed travel records of SARS-CoV-2 positive cases. Thanks to Anna Zhukova, Institut Pasteur for modifying the pastML software to better fit our needs upon request. Finally, sincere thanks to Edyth Parker, Scripps Research, for insightful phylogenetic discussions."],"id":"S04-093.49-010787","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9064402","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35505393","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85129997318","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-e1d96822-d59b-45a3-b51f-6e36f19b02d1","dtu-d4ee83d3-1835-45e8-ad47-e535115bd0ce","ku-51b0d01b-2672-480d-b31c-e83ffa63c4d4","sdu-43413a40-3fef-478a-bbab-354d2e418a06"],"keyword":["COVID-19/epidemiology","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Phylogeny","SARS-CoV-2/genetics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-6B2D322F513D0D7725F93C1C169BC517"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/281354429/s13073_022_01045_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/518917951/s13073_022_01045_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13073-022-01045-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/203034876/s13073_022_01045_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.medrxiv.org/content/10.1101/2021.06.04.21258333v1","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/318706852/Introduction_and_transmission.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering 