{"abstract":"Historically, the psychotherapeutic treatment of psychological problems in old people has had low priority among both clinical psychologists and researchers. Fortunately, this bleak picture is now changing, and a number of reviews and meta-analyses have documented the effect of psychotherapy with older adults suffering from psychopathology such as anxiety or depression. Yet studies on whether older adults not suffering from a psychiatric disorder benefit from psychotherapy are sparse. The objective of this study is threefold: First, we investigate the effects of individual psychotherapy on subjective well-being and symptoms of depression and anxiety of elderly care recipients. Second, we investigate whether the treatment effects continue 3 months after the final treatment session. Third, we examine whether well-being scores improve relatively more than depression and anxiety scores. We found significant positive treatment effects across all measures. Effect sizes were moderate to high. There were no significant differences between posttreatment and follow-up scores, indicating lasting treatment effects. Differences in treatment effect size for our three outcome variables indicated that the WHO-5 scores changed the most, followed by anxiety and depression symptoms. Strengths and weaknesses of the study are discussed, and future directions for research and practice are proposed.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Larsen, Lars","Christoffersen, Morten","Vedel, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-169090"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anxiety","Depression","Elderly people","Well being"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Århus Kommune"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"psychotherapy improves the well being of elderly danish care recipients","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85085765240","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-169090","identifier":[{"id":"85085765240","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-45aaa6de-ebb3-45ba-80e5-5bcd17c32b39"],"keyword":["anxiety","depression","elderly people","gegeropsychology","geropsychology","well-being"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-688B592885F8E4A5E5384A6B507D01AD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus BSS, Department of Psychology and Behavioural Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Århus Kommune"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7bd13f67-d81b-40d2-a742-8115e7100ecb","name":"Larsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-1603-0311","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"cc69f65a-9162-4ebe-8585-b2b3ac5f762d","name":"Christoffersen, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-9423-4654","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vedelpau","last":"Vedel","locid":"717ee2a9-75d4-4f25-987d-96999aad6fee","name":"Vedel, Anna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1024/1662-9647/a000223","issn":["16629647","1662971X"],"issn_org":["16629647"],"issue":"2","journal":"GeroPsych","pages":"67-76","publisher":"Hogrefe Verlag GmbH & Co. KG","status":"p","title":"GeroPsych","volume":"33"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085765240"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-45aaa6de-ebb3-45ba-80e5-5bcd17c32b39"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Psychotherapy Improves the Well-Being of Elderly Danish Care Recipients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-169090","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aims Patients with type 1 diabetes have a high risk of cardiovascular disease. Yet, the importance of routine assessment of myocardial function in patients with type 1 diabetes is not known. Thus, we examined the prognostic importance of NT-proBNP and E/e', an echocardiographic measure of diastolic function, in type 1 diabetes patients with preserved left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) and without known heart disease. Methods and Results Type 1 diabetes patients without known heart disease and LVEF ≥ 45% enrolled in the Thousand and1 study were included and followed through nationwide registries. The risk of major cardiovascular events (MACE) and death associated with levels of NT-proBNP and E/e' was examined. Of 960 patients, median follow-up of 6.3 years (Q1-Q3: 5.7-7.0), 121 (12%) experienced MACE and 51 (5%) died. Increased levels of both NT-proBNP and E/e' were associated with worse outcomes (adjusted hazard ratios for MACE = 1.56 (1.23-1.98) and 4.29 (2.25-8.16) per Loge increase for NT-proBNP and E/e', respectively). NTproBNP and E/e' combined significantly improved the discrimination power of the Steno T1D risk engine (MACE, C-index: 0.813 (0.779-0.847) vs 0.779 (0.742-0.816); P=0.0001; All-cause mortality, C-index 0.855 (0.806-0.903) vs 0.828 (0.776-0.880); P=0.03). Conclusion In patients with type 1 diabetes, preserved ejection fraction, and no known heart disease, NT-proBNP and E/e' were associated with increased risk of MACE and all-cause mortality. The risks associated with NT-proBNP and E/e' combined identified patients at remarkably high risk.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rørth, Rasmus","Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","Andersen, Henrik Ullits","Christoffersen, Christina","Goetze, Jens P.","Køber, Lars","Rossing, Peter","Jensen, Magnus Thorsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-470357"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cardiovascular prognostic value of echocardiography and n terminal pro b type natriuretic peptide in type 000000000001 diabetes the thousand and 000000000001 study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-470357","identifier":[{"id":"85083003356","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32209724","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-8073e03b-b280-4c74-a099-dad03207529c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-91DD0E73F029A0F091AF2609D7E8AB69"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"rørthpau","last":"Rørth","name":"Rørth, Rasmus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter Godsk","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Peter Godsk","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik Ullits","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Henrik Ullits","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Peter","key":"gøtzepau","last":"Gøtze","locid":"980bceaf-dbf3-4f7a-a8d7-0a8e81b638b2","name":"Goetze, Jens P.","name_org":"Gøtze, Jens Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-6356-3829","rank