{"abstract":"Here, we show that the liver-derived apolipoprotein M (ApoM) protects the lung and kidney from pro-fibrotic insults and that this circulating factor is attenuated in aged mice. Aged mouse hepatocytes exhibit transcriptional suppression of ApoM. This leads to reduced sphingosine-1-phosphate (S1P) signaling via the S1P receptor 1 (S1PR1) in the vascular endothelial cells of lung and kidney. Suboptimal S1PR1 angiocrine signaling causes reduced resistance to injury-induced vascular leak and leads to organ fibrosis. Plasma transfusion from Apom transgenic mice but not Apom knockout mice blocked fibrosis in the lung. Similarly, infusion of recombinant therapeutics, ApoM-Fc fusion protein enhanced kidney and lung regeneration and attenuated fibrosis in aged mouse after injury. Furthermore, we identified that aging alters Sirtuin-1-hepatic nuclear factor 4α circuit in hepatocytes to downregulate ApoM. These data reveal an integrative organ adaptation that involves circulating S1P chaperone ApoM+ high density lipoprotein (HDL), which signals via endothelial niche S1PR1 to spur regeneration over fibrosis.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Ding, Bi Sen","Yang, Dawei","Swendeman, Steve L.","Christoffersen, Christina","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Friedman, Scott L.","Powell, Charles A.","Hla, Timothy","Cao, Zhongwei"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-466177"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Cornell University","Harvard University","Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai"],"keyword":["Aging","Endothelial cell","Fibrosis","Lipoprotein","kidney repair"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"aging suppresses sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate chaperone apom in circulation resulting in maladaptive organ repair","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7607448/pdf/nihms-1638874.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-466177","identifier":[{"id":"85086602840","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32544390","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7607448","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-798193ee-e4b7-40c6-a209-4f1cd75a8e38"],"keyword":["aging","endothelial cell","fibrosis","kidney repair","lipoprotein","lung regeneration","sphingosine-1-phosphate receptor","vascular barrier","vascular niche"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77393A505065DEC81848E9F52873F595"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7607448/pdf/nihms-1638874.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"icahn school of medicine at mount sinai","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Icahn School of Medicine at Mount Sinai","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"cornell university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Cornell University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Bi Sen","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Bi Sen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dawei","key":"yangpau","last":"Yang","name":"Yang, Dawei","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Steve L.","key":"swendemanpau","last":"Swendeman","name":"Swendeman, Steve L.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Lars B.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, Lars B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Scott L.","key":"friedmanpau","last":"Friedman","name":"Friedman, Scott L.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Charles A.","key":"powellpau","last":"Powell","name":"Powell, Charles A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Timothy","key":"hlapau","last":"Hla","name":"Hla, Timothy","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Zhongwei","key":"caopau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Zhongwei","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32544390"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.devcel.2020.05.024","issn":["15345807","18781551"],"issn_org":["15345807"],"issue":"6","journal":"Developmental Cell","pages":"677-690","status":"p","title":"Developmental Cell","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85086602840"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-798193ee-e4b7-40c6-a209-4f1cd75a8e38"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Aging Suppresses Sphingosine-1-Phosphate Chaperone ApoM in Circulation Resulting in Maladaptive Organ Repair","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-466177","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Context: Recent studies have discovered a role of apolipoprotein M (apoM) in energy metabolism, and observational analyses in humans suggest an association with type 2 diabetes. The causal relationship remains however elusive. Objective: To investigate whether reduced plasma apoM concentrations are causally linked to increased risk of type 2 diabetes. Design: Prospective study design analyzed by Mendelian randomization. Setting and participants: Two cohorts reflecting the Danish general population: the Copenhagen City Heart Study (CCHS, n = 8589) and the Copenhagen General Population Study (CGPS; n = 93 857). Observational analyses included a subset of participants from the CCHS with available plasma apoM (n = 725). Genetic analyses included the complete cohorts (n = 102 446). During a median follow-up of 16 years (CCHS) and 8 years (CGPS), 563 and 2132 participants developed type 2 diabetes. Main outcome measures: Plasma apoM concentration, genetic variants in APOM, and type 2 diabetes. Results: First, we identified an inverse correlation between plasma apoM and risk of type 2 diabetes in a subset of participants from the CCHS (hazard ratio between highest vs lowest quartile (reference) = 0.32; 95% confidence interval = 0.1-1.01; P for trend = .02). Second, genotyping of specific single nucleotide polymorphisms in APOM further revealed a 10.8% (P = 6.2 x 10(-5)) reduced plasma apoM concentration in participants with variant rs1266078. Third, a meta-analysis including data from 599 451 individuals showed no association between rs1266078 and risk of type 2 diabetes. Conclusions: The present study does not appear to support a causal association between plasma apoM and risk of type 2 diabetes.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hajny, Stefan","Christoffersen, Mette","Dalila, Nawar","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Christoffersen, Christina"],"cuid":["S02-097.68-017696"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Christoffersen, Christina"],"keyword":["Apolipoproteins","Association","Cholesterol","Coronary heart disease","Genetics","Insulin Resistance","Lipids","Mendelian randomization","Metabolism","Plasma","Receptor","Type 2 diabetes","apoM"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"apolipoprotein m and risk of type 000000000002 diabetes","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85089128391","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-097.68-017696","identifier":[{"id":"85089128391","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000574866500071","type":"wos"},{"id":"32621749","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-455b6f35-60bc-4f3f-98f9-8da6580dac43","ku-f39d15fd-af66-48b8-9930-a4ee2d6a574b"],"keyword":["APOM","ASSOCIATION","Apolipoproteins","CHOLESTEROL","CORONARY-HEART-DISEASE","Genetics","INSULIN-RESISTANCE","LIPIDS","METABOLISM","Mendelian randomization","PLASMA","RECEPTOR","Type 2 diabetes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0CEBEE1C293054A5F99D59A4EF3D5FB3"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Deans Office, Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Stefan","key":"hajnystefanpau","last":"Hajny","locid":"ef875bee-127b-4174-bd30-ae63a72d91d0","name":"Hajny, Stefan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"christoffersenmettepau","last":"Christoffersen","name":"Christoffersen, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nawar","key":"dalilanawarpau","last":"Dalila","name":"Dalila, Nawar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars B.","key":"nielsenlarsbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0d69b83d-4fd2-46ea-9855-44ce4e1c8f38","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, Lars B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars B.","key":"nielsenlarsbpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lars B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"tybjærghansenannepau","last":"Tybjaerg-Hansen","locid":"452a492e-c869-41e5-b60e-1d2a542287cf","name":"Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","name_org":"Tybjaerg-Hansen, Anne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenchristinapau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32621749"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgaa433","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"3046-3057","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology & Metabolism","volume":"105"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85089128391"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-455b6f35-60bc-4f3f-98f9-8da6580dac43","ku-f39d15fd-af66-48b8-9930-a4ee2d6a574b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Apolipoprotein M and Risk of Type 2 Diabetes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.68-017696","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Objective: The axis of apolipoprotein M (apoM) and sphingosine-1-phosphate (S1P) is of importance to plasma lipid levels, endothelial function, and development of atherosclerosis. Menopause is accompanied by dyslipidemia and an increased risk of atherosclerosis, which can be lowered by exercise training. The aim of this study was to explore if effects of menopause and training are paralleled by changes in the apoM/S1P axis. Methods: Healthy, late premenopausal (n=38, age 49.2±2) and recent postmenopausal (n=37, age 53.3±3) women from the Copenhagen Women Study participated in a three-month, aerobic high-intensity exercise intervention. Results: Before training, plasma apoM was higher in postmenopausal (1.08±0.2 µmol/l (mean±SD)) compared to premenopausal (0.82±0.2 µmol/l) women (p<0.0001). Plasma S1P was similar in the two groups (0.44±0.1 and 0.46±0.1 µmol/l, respectively). Hence, the pre-training S1P/apoM ratio was 26% lower in postmenopausal than premenopausal women (p<0.0001). After the training program, plasma apoM increased from 0.82±0.2 to 0.90±0.3 µmol/l in premenopausal women and from 1.08±0.2 to 1.16±0.3 µmol/l in postmenopausal women (p<0.05). Plasma S1P increased from 0.44±0.1 to 0.47±0.1 µmol/l in premenopausal women and from 0.46±0.1 to 0.48±0.1 µmol/l in postmenopausal women (p<0.05). Conclusions: The results suggest that menopause is accompanied by higher plasma apoM but not S1P concentrations, and that exercise training increases plasma apoM and S1P in healthy middle-aged women irrespective of menopausal status.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Yafasova, Adelina","Mandrup, Camilla Maria","Egelund, Jon","Nyberg, Michael Permin","Stallknecht, Bente","Hellsten, Ylva","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Christoffersen, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-468164"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Apolipoproteins","Atherosclerosis","Cardiovascular training","Faculty of Science","Lipids","Lipoprotein metabolism","Sphingolipids"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of menopause and exercise training on plasma apolipoprotein m and sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248819670/Effect_of_menopause_and_exercise_training_on_plasma_apolipoprotein_M_and_sphingosine_1_phosphate_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-468164","identifier":[{"id":"30433864","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85060819368","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-7cc044f5-2419-4c7d-92bf-98794e6b9037"],"keyword":["Apolipoproteins","Atherosclerosis","Cardiovascular training","Faculty of Science","Lipids","Lipoprotein metabolism","Menopausal transition","Sphingolipids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49FFBDB7C4C8FAA1F8463DAE5DECBC31"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/248819670/Effect_of_menopause_and_exercise_training_on_plasma_apolipoprotein_M_and_sphingosine_1_phosphate_accepted_version_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Adelina","key":"yafasovapau","last":"Yafasova","name":"Yafasova, Adelina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Camilla Maria","key":"mandruppau","last":"Mandrup","locid":"7dc1cc65-c77a-4a36-9a2b-9eafda518d47","name":"Mandrup, Camilla Maria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jon","key":"egelundpau","last":"Egelund","locid":"b1d76378-3e05-496b-bc2f-6f8d44f10bc1","name":"Egelund, Jon","orcid":"0000-0003-4353-0362","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Michael Permin","key":"nybergpau","last":"Nyberg","locid":"3a44876c-6484-4899-ade6-7e80d0483f3d","name":"Nyberg, Michael Permin","orcid":"0000-0002-3937-4697","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Bente","key":"stallknechtpau","last":"Stallknecht","locid":"eddf86eb-44d6-44ca-985b-79a29dd3cec7","name":"Stallknecht, Bente","orcid":"0000-0003-3117-0451","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Ylva","key":"hellstenpau","last":"Hellsten","locid":"902a8d03-73c1-41fa-a0a3-7f250470e2f0","name":"Hellsten, Ylva","orcid":"0000-0002-2435-9558","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30433864"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1152/japplphysiol.00527.2018","issn":["15221601","87507587"],"issn_org":["87507587"],"issue":"1","journal":"Journal of Applied Physiology","pages":"214-220","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Physiology","volume":"126"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060819368"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7cc044f5-2419-4c7d-92bf-98794e6b9037"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Effect of menopause and exercise training on plasma apolipoprotein M and sphingosine-1-phosphate","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-468164","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Obesity and diabetes in humans are associated with hypertrophic remodeling and increased media:lumen ratio of small resistance arteries, which is an independent predictor of cardiovascular events. In order to minimize increases in media:lumen ratio, hypertrophic remodeling should be accompanied by outward remodeling. We aimed to investigate the mechanisms of structural remodeling in small pial arteries (PA) and terminal mesenteric arteries (TMA) from obese Göttingen Minipigs with or without diabetes. Göttingen Minipigs received either control diet (LC), high fat/high fructose/high cholesterol diet (FFC), or FFC diet with streptozotocin-induced diabetes (FFC/STZ) for 13 months. At study end (20 months), we assessed body weight, fasting plasma biochemistry, passive vessel dimensions, mRNA expression (MMP2, MMP9, TIMP1, TGM2, ROCK1, TGFBR2, and IGFR1 genes), and immunofluorescence in PAs and TMAs. We performed multiple linear correlation analyses using plasma values, structural data, and gene expression data. We detected outward hypertrophic remodeling in TMAs and hypertrophic remodeling in PAs from FFC/STZ animals. ROCK1 and TGM2 genes were up-regulated in PAs and TMAs from the FFC/STZ group. Passive lumen diameter of TMAs was correlated with plasma values of glucose, fructosamine, total cholesterol, and triglycerides. ROCK1 and TGM2 expressions in TMAs were correlated with passive lumen diameter, plasma glucose, fructosamine, and total cholesterol. ROCK1 and TGM2 proteins were immunolocalized in the media of PAs and TMAs, and their fluorescence levels were increased in the FFC/STZ group. Hyperglycemia/hyperlipidemia is involved in regulation of ROCK1 and TGM2 expression leading to outward remodeling of small resistance arteries in obese diabetic Göttingen Minipigs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Ludvigsen, Trine Pagh","Olsen, Lisbeth Høier","Pedersen, Henrik Duelund","Østergaard Christoffersen, Berit","Jensen, Lars Jørn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-535085"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diabetes","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Göttingen minipigs","Obesity","Remodeling","Resistance arteries","Transglutaminase 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hyperglycemia induced transcriptional regulation of rock000000000001 and tgm000000000002 expression is involved in small artery remodeling in obese diabetic göttingen minipigs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-535085","identifier":[{"id":"31830262","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85077173657","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ed4b526e-5472-4a9e-8ad3-8b1e5c37940a"],"keyword":["Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Göttingen minipigs","Rho-kinase 1","Transglutaminase 2","diabetes","obesity","remodeling","resistance arteries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9E26C308E7D4CA6CF4B3EB67D85656EA"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Lifepharm","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Preclinical Disease Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Trine Pagh","key":"ludvigsenpau","last":"Ludvigsen","name":"Ludvigsen, Trine Pagh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lisbeth Høier","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"a30ce7a9-ef18-475f-a860-819856d64d5a","name":"Olsen, Lisbeth Høier","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henrik Duelund","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"15c9727b-7ebe-4def-8eb3-22388fe24565","name":"Pedersen, Henrik Duelund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Berit","key":"østergaardchristoffersenpau","last":"Østergaard Christoffersen","name":"Østergaard Christoffersen, Berit","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Jørn","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"8de80477-3346-487d-bf10-bfc8e7890e42","name":"Jensen, Lars Jørn","orcid":"0000-0003-4559-7456","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31830262"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1042/cs20191066","issn":["01435221","14708736"],"issn_org":["01435221"],"issue":"24","journal":"Clinical Science","pages":"2499-2516","status":"p","title":"Clinical Science","volume":"133"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85077173657"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ed4b526e-5472-4a9e-8ad3-8b1e5c37940a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hyperglycemia-induced transcriptional regulation of ROCK1 and TGM2 expression is involved in small artery remodeling in obese diabetic Göttingen Minipigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-535085","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
