{"abstract":"Chronic kidney disease affects as much as 13% of the population, and is associated with a markedly increased risk of developing cardiovascular disease. One of the underlying reasons is accelerated development of atherosclerosis. This can be ascribed both to increased occurrence of traditional cardiovascular risk factors, and to risk factors that may be unique to patients with chronic kidney disease. The latter is reflected in the observation that the current treatment modalities, mainly directed against traditional risk factors, are insufficient to prevent cardiovascular disease in the patient with chronic kidney disease. This review discusses mechanisms accelerating uremic atherosclerosis with a specific focus on the putative roles of apolipoprotein(apo)s B and M that may be particularly important in patients with chronic kidney disease.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Christina","Bartels, Emil D.","Pedersen, Annemarie Aarup","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Pedersen, Tanja Xenia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-479896"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["ApoB","Atherosclerosis","Lipoprotein a","S1P","Uremia","apoM"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"apob and apom new aspects of lipoprotein biology in uremia induced atherosclerosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-479896","identifier":[{"id":"28351665","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85016566112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-90b38ed3-581c-4ca7-8fdc-1449f79bc955"],"keyword":["ApoB","ApoM","Atherosclerosis","Lipoprotein(a)","S1P","Uremia"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8EC0A3236267D5758D10F74783F2C966"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenchristinapau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Emil D.","key":"bartelsemildpau","last":"Bartels","locid":"93bf9a38-d3f8-45fd-8c88-ab365982b098","name":"Bartels, Emil D.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Annemarie Aarup","key":"pedersenannemarieaaruppau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d8f930f5-b2a7-41e2-b558-9e91197b1c6b","name":"Pedersen, Annemarie Aarup","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenlarsbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tanja X.","key":"pedersentanjaxeniapau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"78b12e4c-f5b0-433c-adae-ee24837bb372","name":"Pedersen, Tanja Xenia","name_org":"Pedersen, Tanja X.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28351665"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejphar.2017.03.053","issn":["00142999","18790712"],"issn_org":["00142999"],"journal":"European Journal of Pharmacology","pages":"154-160","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Pharmacology","volume":"816"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85016566112"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-90b38ed3-581c-4ca7-8fdc-1449f79bc955"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"ApoB and apoM - New aspects of lipoprotein biology in uremia-induced atherosclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-479896","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: Atherosclerotic lesions contain hypoxic areas, but the pathophysiological importance of hypoxia is unknown. Hypoxia-inducible factor-1α (HIF-1α) is a key transcription factor in cellular responses to hypoxia. We investigated the hypothesis that HIF-1α has effects on macrophage biology that promotes atherogenesis in mice. APPROACH AND RESULTS: Studies with molecular probes, immunostaining, and laser microdissection of aortas revealed abundant hypoxic, HIF-1α-expressing macrophages in murine atherosclerotic lesions. To investigate the significance of macrophage HIF-1α, Ldlr(-/-) mice were transplanted with bone marrow from mice with HIF-1α deficiency in the myeloid cells or control bone marrow. The HIF-1α deficiency in myeloid cells reduced atherosclerosis in aorta of the Ldlr(-/-) recipient mice by ≈72% (P=0.006).In vitro, HIF-1α-deficient macrophages displayed decreased differentiation to proinflammatory M1 macrophages and reduced expression of inflammatory genes. HIF-1α deficiency also affected glucose uptake, apoptosis, and migratory abilities of the macrophages. CONCLUSIONS: HIF-1α expression in macrophages affects their intrinsic inflammatory profile and promotes development of atherosclerosis.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Annemarie Aarup","Pedersen, Tanja Xenia","Nielsen, Nanna Maria Junker","Christoffersen, Christina","Bartels, Emil D.","Madsen, Marie","Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","Nielsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-403344"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hypoxia inducible factor 000000000001α expression in macrophages promotes development of atherosclerosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-403344","identifier":[{"id":"84979662970","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27444197","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-10c0a268-f67c-4b7d-ab98-779d293fbfb2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77A8139F30186025F5EFB78A871B2D45"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Annemarie Aarup","key":"pedersenannemarieaaruppau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"d8f930f5-b2a7-41e2-b558-9e91197b1c6b","name":"Pedersen, Annemarie Aarup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tanja X","key":"pedersentanjaxeniapau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"78b12e4c-f5b0-433c-adae-ee24837bb372","name":"Pedersen, Tanja Xenia","name_org":"Pedersen, Tanja X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nanna","key":"nielsennannamariajunkerpau","last":"Junker","locid":"a35e2345-80ff-4554-aad3-92023fa268b8","name":"Nielsen, Nanna Maria Junker","name_org":"Junker, Nanna","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenchristinapau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Emil D","key":"bartelsemildpau","last":"Bartels","locid":"93bf9a38-d3f8-45fd-8c88-ab365982b098","name":"Bartels, Emil D.","name_org":"Bartels, Emil D","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"madsenmariepau","last":"Madsen","locid":"2552b6c8-6b3a-41c7-aec6-bb2be67d1bf1","name":"Madsen, Marie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten H","key":"nielsencarstenhaagenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"aefb223a-8c5c-41c6-9e69-fade0a04bf90","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Haagen","name_org":"Nielsen, Carsten H","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenlarsbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27444197"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/atvbaha.116.307830","issn":["10795642","15244636"],"issn_org":["10795642"],"issue":"9","journal":"Arteriosclerosis, Thrombosis, and Vascular Biology","pages":"1782-1790","status":"p","title":"Arteriosclerosis, Thrombosis, and Vascular Biology","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84979662970"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-10c0a268-f67c-4b7d-ab98-779d293fbfb2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hypoxia-Inducible Factor-1α Expression in Macrophages Promotes Development of Atherosclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-403344","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Regeneration of hepatic sinusoidal vasculature is essential for non-fibrotic liver regrowth and restoration of its metabolic capacity. However, little is known about how this specialized vascular niche is regenerated. Here we show that activation of endothelial sphingosine-1-phosphate receptor-1 (S1P1) by its natural ligand bound to HDL (HDL-S1P) induces liver regeneration and curtails fibrosis. In mice lacking HDL-S1P, liver regeneration after partial hepatectomy was impeded and associated with aberrant vascular remodeling, thrombosis and peri-sinusoidal fibrosis. Notably, this \"maladaptive repair\" phenotype was recapitulated in mice that lack S1P1 in the endothelium. Reciprocally, enhanced plasma levels of HDL-S1P or administration of SEW2871, a pharmacological agonist specific for S1P1 enhanced regeneration of metabolically functional vasculature and alleviated fibrosis in mouse chronic injury and cholestasis models. This study shows that natural and pharmacological ligands modulate endothelial S1P1 to stimulate liver regeneration and inhibit fibrosis, suggesting that activation of this pathway may be a novel therapeutic strategy for liver fibrosis.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Ding, Bi-Sen","Liu, Catherine H","Sun, Yue","Chen, Yutian","Swendeman, Steven L","Jung, Bongnam","Chavez, Deebly","Cao, Zhongwei","Christoffersen, Christina","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Schwab, Susan R","Rafii, Shahin","Hla, Timothy"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-491283"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hdl activation of endothelial sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate receptor 000000000001 s000000000001p000000000001 promotes regeneration and suppresses fibrosis in the liver","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-491283","identifier":[{"id":"85079726211","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28018969","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5161208","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a3c6e2fa-be55-46d0-b578-610c4f0c41ff"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5760C45E0FA6B5D0510EEF7423C085A5"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Bi-Sen","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, Bi-Sen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Catherine H","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Catherine H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yue","key":"sunpau","last":"Sun","name":"Sun, Yue","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yutian","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Yutian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steven L","key":"swendemanpau","last":"Swendeman","name":"Swendeman, Steven L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bongnam","key":"jungpau","last":"Jung","name":"Jung, Bongnam","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Deebly","key":"chavezpau","last":"Chavez","name":"Chavez, Deebly","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Zhongwei","key":"caopau","last":"Cao","name":"Cao, Zhongwei","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susan R","key":"schwabpau","last":"Schwab","name":"Schwab, Susan R","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Shahin","key":"rafiipau","last":"Rafii","name":"Rafii, Shahin","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Timothy","key":"hlapau","last":"Hla","name":"Hla, Timothy","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28018969"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1172/jci.insight.87058","issn":["23793708"],"issue":"21","journal":"JCI Insight","paperid":"e87058","status":"p","title":"JCI Insight","title_org":"JCI insight","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079726211"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a3c6e2fa-be55-46d0-b578-610c4f0c41ff"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"HDL activation of endothelial sphingosine-1-phosphate receptor-1 (S1P1) promotes regeneration and suppresses fibrosis in the liver","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-491283","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
