{"abstract":"Apolipoprotein M (ApoM) transports sphingosine-1-phosphate (S1P) in plasma, and ApoM-deficient mice (Apom(-/-)) have ∼50% reduced plasma S1P levels. There are 5 known S1P receptors, and S1P induces adherens junction formation between endothelial cells through the S1P1 receptor, which in turn suppresses vascular leak. Increased vascular permeability is a hallmark of inflammation. The purpose of this study was to explore the relationships between vascular leakage in ApoM deficiency and S1P1 function in normal physiology and in inflammation. Vascular permeability in the lungs was assessed by accumulation of dextran molecules (70 kDa) and was increased ∼40% in Apom(-/-) mice compared to WT (C57Bl6/j) mice. Reconstitution of plasma ApoM/S1P or treatment with an S1P1 receptor agonist (SEW2871) rapidly reversed the vascular leakage to a level similar to that in WT mice, suggesting that it is caused by decreased plasma levels of S1P and reduced S1P1 stimulation. In a carrageenan-induced model of inflammation, Apom(-/-) mice had increased vascular leakage compared with that in WT mice. Adenoviral overexpression of ApoM in Apom(-/-) mice decreased the vascular leakage compared to adenoviral overexpression of green fluorescent protein. The study suggests that vascular leakage of albumin-sized particles in ApoM deficiency is S1P- and S1P1-dependent and this dependency exacerbates the response to inflammatory stimuli.-Christensen, P. M., Liu, C. H., Swendeman, S. L., Obinata, H., Qvortrup, K., Nielsen, L B., Hla, T., Di Lorenzo, A., Christoffersen, C. Impaired endothelial barrier function in apolipoprotein M-deficient mice is dependent on sphingosine-1-phosphate receptor 1.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Christensen, Pernille Melia","Liu, Catherine H","Swendeman, Steven L","Obinata, Hideru","Qvortrup, Klaus","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Hla, Timothy","Di Lorenzo, Annarita","Christoffersen, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516624"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impaired endothelial barrier function in apolipoprotein m deficient mice is dependent on sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate receptor 000000000001","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-516624","identifier":[{"id":"26956418","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4871798","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84973174711","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ce2f7d80-c0f3-4707-ae94-318a76ba9fef"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-63698B5D358A82F0784EA374067DEE2F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille M","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"af15030e-550e-4ad8-9cd1-ae8d164c08b2","name":"Christensen, Pernille Melia","name_org":"Christensen, Pernille M","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Catherine H","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Catherine H","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steven L","key":"swendemanpau","last":"Swendeman","name":"Swendeman, Steven L","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hideru","key":"obinatapau","last":"Obinata","name":"Obinata, Hideru","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Klaus","key":"qvortruppau","last":"Qvortrup","locid":"e7d5e238-9367-4780-9b26-e468bcdff739","name":"Qvortrup, Klaus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Timothy","key":"hlapau","last":"Hla","name":"Hla, Timothy","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Annarita","key":"dilorenzopau","last":"Di Lorenzo","name":"Di Lorenzo, Annarita","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26956418"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1096/fj.201500064","issn":["08926638","15306860"],"issn_org":["08926638"],"issue":"6","journal":"FASEB Journal","pages":"2351-2359","status":"p","title":"FASEB Journal","title_org":"FASEB journal : official publication of the Federation of American Societies for Experimental Biology","volume":"30"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84973174711"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ce2f7d80-c0f3-4707-ae94-318a76ba9fef"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Impaired endothelial barrier function in apolipoprotein M-deficient mice is dependent on sphingosine-1-phosphate receptor 1","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-516624","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"AIM: Increasing evidence points to lipoprotein composition rather than reverse cholesterol transport in the cardioprotective properties of high-density lipoproteins (HDL). HDL binding to receptors at the surface of cardiomyocytes activates signalling pathways promoting survival, but downstream targets are largely unknown. Here, we investigate the pathways by which the Sphingosine-1-Phosphate (S1P) constituent of HDL limits cell death induced by cardiac ischemia/reperfusion (I/R). METHODS AND RESULTS: Apolipoprotein M (ApoM) transgenic (Apom-Tg) mice, in which plasma S1P is increased by 296%, and wild-type (WT) mice were subjected to in vivo I/R. Infarct size, neutrophil infiltration into the infarcted area and serum Troponin I were less pronounced in Apom-Tg mice. In vitro experiments suggest that this cardioprotection depends on direct effects of S1P on cardiomyocytes, whereas leukocyte recruitment seems only indirectly affected. Importantly, short-term S1P treatment at the onset of reperfusion was sufficient to reduce ischemia/reperfusion injury in isolated perfused hearts. Mechanistic in vitro and ex vivo studies revealed that 5 min of S1P treatment induced phosphorylation of the gap junction protein Connexin43 (Cx43) on Serine368, which was mediated by S1P2 and S1P3, but not by S1P1, receptors in cardiomyocytes. Finally, S1P-induced reduction of infarct size after ex vivo I/R was lost in hearts of mice with a truncated C-terminus of Cx43 (Cx43(K258/KO)) or in which the Serine368 is mutated to a non-phosphorylatable Alanine (Cx43(S368A/S368A)). CONCLUSION: Our study reveals an important molecular pathway by which modulating the apoM/S1P axis has a therapeutic potential in the fight against ischemia/reperfusion injury in the heart.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Morel, Sandrine","Christoffersen, Christina","Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","Montecucco, Fabrizio","Rochemont, Viviane","Frias, Miguel A","Mach, Francois","James, Richard W","Naus, Christian C","Chanson, Marc","Lampe, Paul D","Nielsen, Morten Schak","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Kwak, Brenda R"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-405644"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate reduces ischemia reperfusion injury by phosphorylating the gap junction protein connexin000000000043","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-405644","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4752044","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84959922603","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26762268","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-147a6e11-0e8c-456b-94cf-d22eea497242"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F5B75C2E11C69E9610B4E8B9DE3715F8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Sandrine","key":"morelsandrinepau","last":"Morel","name":"Morel, Sandrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenchristinapau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lene N","key":"axelsenlenenygaardpau","last":"Axelsen","locid":"2632f623-a6d6-49e1-884c-0560715787be","name":"Axelsen, Lene Nygaard","name_org":"Axelsen, Lene N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Fabrizio","key":"montecuccofabriziopau","last":"Montecucco","name":"Montecucco, Fabrizio","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Viviane","key":"rochemontvivianepau","last":"Rochemont","name":"Rochemont, Viviane","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Miguel A","key":"friasmiguelapau","last":"Frias","name":"Frias, Miguel A","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Francois","key":"machfrancoispau","last":"Mach","name":"Mach, Francois","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Richard W","key":"jamesrichardwpau","last":"James","name":"James, Richard W","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian C","key":"nauschristiancpau","last":"Naus","name":"Naus, Christian C","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marc","key":"chansonmarcpau","last":"Chanson","name":"Chanson, Marc","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Paul D","key":"lampepauldpau","last":"Lampe","name":"Lampe, Paul D","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten S","key":"nielsenmortenschakpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b203113e-fe9b-4863-8eb0-3022ca8cc9e2","name":"Nielsen, Morten Schak","name_org":"Nielsen, Morten S","orcid":"0000-0002-9718-5421","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars B","key":"nielsenlarsbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, Lars B","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Brenda R","key":"kwakbrendarpau","last":"Kwak","name":"Kwak, Brenda R","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26762268"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/cvr/cvw004","issn":["00086363","17553245"],"issn_org":["00086363"],"journal":"Cardiovascular Research","pages":"385-396","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Research","volume":"109"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84959922603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-147a6e11-0e8c-456b-94cf-d22eea497242"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Sphingosine-1-Phosphate reduces ischemia/reperfusion injury by phosphorylating the gap junction protein Connexin43","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-405644","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Human genetics studies have implicated GALNT2, encoding GalNAc-T2, as a regulator of high-density lipoprotein cholesterol (HDL-C) metabolism, but the mechanisms relating GALNT2 to HDL-C remain unclear. We investigated the impact of homozygous GALNT2 deficiency on HDL-C in humans and mammalian models. We identified two humans homozygous for loss-of-function mutations in GALNT2 who demonstrated low HDL-C. We also found that GALNT2 loss of function in mice, rats, and nonhuman primates decreased HDL-C. O-glycoproteomics studies of a human GALNT2-deficient subject validated ANGPTL3 and ApoC-III as GalNAc-T2 targets. Additional glycoproteomics in rodents identified targets influencing HDL-C, including phospholipid transfer protein (PLTP). GALNT2 deficiency reduced plasma PLTP activity in humans and rodents, and in mice this was rescued by reconstitution of hepatic Galnt2. We also found that GALNT2 GWAS SNPs associated with reduced HDL-C also correlate with lower hepatic GALNT2 expression. These results posit GALNT2 as a direct modulator of HDL metabolism across mammals.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Khetarpal, Sumeet A","Schjoldager, Katrine T.","Christoffersen, Christina","Raghavan, Avanthi","Edmondson, Andrew C","Reutter, Heiko M","Ahmed, Bouhouche","Ouazzani, Reda","Peloso, Gina M","Vitali, Cecilia","Zhao, Wei","Somasundara, Amritha Varshini Hanasoge","Millar, John S","Park, YoSon","Fernando, Gayani","Livanov, Valentin","Choi, Seungbum","Noé, Eric","Patel, Pritesh","Ho, Siew Peng","Kirchgessner, Todd G","Wandall, Hans H","Hansen, Lars","Bennett, Eric P","Vakhrushev, Sergey Y.","Saleheen, Danish","Kathiresan, Sekar","Brown, Christopher D","Abou Jamra, Rami","LeGuern, Eric","Clausen, Henrik","Rader, Daniel J"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-516484"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bonn","University of Pennsylvania"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"loss of function of galnt000000000002 lowers high density lipoproteins in humans nonhuman primates and rodents","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-516484","identifier":[{"id":"84991044385","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27508872","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-cdf60c81-c11c-451b-b617-36d368f7ccca"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DFD5BBA7734D0D82FD5123B25722F7E8"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"university of pennsylvania","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Pennsylvania","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Glycomics Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bonn","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sumeet A","key":"khetarpalpau","last":"Khetarpal","name":"Khetarpal, Sumeet A","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katrine T","key":"schjoldagerpau","last":"Schjoldager","locid":"299ad5aa-0120-471e-bf90-5e688fea7d0b","name":"Schjoldager, Katrine T.","name_org":"Schjoldager, Katrine T","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen",