12","issn":["15504131","19327420"],"issn_org":["15504131"],"issue":"2","journal":"Cell Metabolism","pages":"234-245","status":"p","title":"Cell Metabolism","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991044385"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-cdf60c81-c11c-451b-b617-36d368f7ccca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Loss of Function of GALNT2 Lowers High-Density Lipoproteins in Humans, Nonhuman Primates, and Rodents","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-516484","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"apoM is a member of the lipocalin superfamily and circulates in plasma attached to HDL particles. apoM plays a role in cholesterol metabolism and has recently been identified as transporter for the signaling lipid, sphingosine-1-phosphate (S1P), in plasma. S1P is implicated in several inflammatory diseases such as multiple sclerosis and rheumatoid arthritis. The ability to accurately measure apoM is crucial for investigating its biological functions and possible clinical implications. However, reliable commercial methods have been lacking so far. Therefore, we have developed an assay that specifically recognizes human apoM in plasma using commercially available reagents. Commercial apoM antibodies were screened for compatibility in a sandwich ELISA-based assay. One optimal pair of antibodies was chosen, and sample preparation, buffers, and incubation times were optimized to generate a simple and reproducible method. Validation and comparison to a previously described ELISA for apoM confirmed that the assay displays a high degree of sensitivity, specificity, and precision. Our results show that commercially available antibodies can be used to accurately measure human plasma apoM. This method can be implemented in every laboratory and will help promote high quality research.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bosteen, Markus Høybye","Dahlbäck, Björn","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Christoffersen, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-440495"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"protein unfolding allows use of commercial antibodies in an apolipoprotein m sandwich elisa","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1194/jlr.D055947","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-440495","identifier":[{"id":"84925307845","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25561460","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4340322","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4ed8473d-67eb-4e8e-a32e-866ae565ac3c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-43768CC1F81C295FAA0479DEE49B3874"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1194/jlr.D055947","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Markus Høybye","key":"bosteenpau","last":"Bosteen","locid":"9230f6f3-c9a1-48a4-bd1c-a00e5469c72c","name":"Bosteen, Markus Høybye","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Björn","key":"dahlbäckpau","last":"Dahlbäck","name":"Dahlbäck, Björn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25561460"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1194/jlr.d055947","issn":["00222275","15397262"],"issn_org":["00222275"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Lipid Research","pages":"754-759","status":"p","title":"Journal of Lipid Research","volume":"56"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925307845"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4ed8473d-67eb-4e8e-a32e-866ae565ac3c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Protein unfolding allows use of commercial antibodies in an apolipoprotein M sandwich ELISA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-440495","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Conventional laparoscopic cholecystectomy (CLC) is regarded as the gold standard for cholecystectomy. However, single-incision laparoscopic cholecystectomy (SLC) has been suggested to replace CLC. This study aimed at comparing long-term incidences of port-site hernia and chronic pain after SLC versus CLC. METHODS: We conducted a matched cohort study based on prospective data (Jan 1, 2009-June 1, 2011) from the Danish Cholecystectomy Database with perioperative information and clinical follow-up. Consecutive patients undergoing elective SLC during the study period were included and matched 1:2 with patients subjected to CLC using pre-defined criteria. Follow-up data were obtained from the Danish National Patient Registry, mailed patient questionnaires, and clinical examination. A port-site hernia was defined as a repair for a port-site hernia or clinical hernia located at one or more port sites. RESULTS: In total, 699 patients were eligible and 147 patients were excluded from the analysis due to pre-defined criteria. The rate of returned questionnaires was 83%. Thus, 552 (SLC, n = 185; CLC, n = 367) patients were analyzed. The median observation time was 48 months (range 1-65) after SLC and 48 months (1-64) after CLC (P = 0.940). The total cumulated port-site hernia rate was 4 % and 6 % for SLC and CLC, respectively (P = 0.560). Incidences of moderate/severe chronic pain were 4 % and 5 % after SLC and CLC, respectively (P = 0.661). CONCLUSIONS: We found no difference in long-term incidence of port-site hernia or chronic pain after SLC versus CLC.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Mette W","Brandt, Erik","Oehlenschläger, Jacob","Rosenberg, Jacob","Helgstrand, Frederik","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Bardram, Linda","Bisgaard, Thue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-483721"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no difference in incidence of port site hernia and chronic pain after single incision laparoscopic cholecystectomy versus conventional laparoscopic cholecystectomy a nationwide prospective matched cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-483721","identifier":[{"id":"25612547","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84944353833","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-970ef4ca-9a71-4e7f-aa47-f535021dbe51"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-27D545C417A2AD8D1C5048EF60E26723"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Mette W","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","name":"Christoffersen, Mette W","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Erik","key":"brandtpau","last":"Brandt","name":"Brandt, Erik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob","key":"oehlenschlägerpau","last":"Oehlenschläger","name":"Oehlenschläger, Jacob","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob","key":"rosenbergpau","last":"Rosenberg","locid":"00b94c43-5ffb-4e1e-ac75-320aa0c79745","name":"Rosenberg, Jacob","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik","key":"helgstrandpau","last":"Helgstrand","locid":"32f3911d-c68c-46a4-84de-2b90d8be2614","name":"Helgstrand, Frederik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","fi