 Seier","orcid":"0000-0003-4419-4911","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Steffen Robert","key":"eickhardtsørensenpau","last":"Eickhardt-Sørensen","locid":"3bcbf028-fd14-48ec-89a7-8319d3ff873f","name":"Eickhardt-Dalbøge, Steffen Robert","name_org":"Eickhardt-Sørensen, Steffen Robert","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Hannah","key":"trostruppau","last":"Trostrup","name":"Trostrup, Hannah","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","name":"Christoffersen, Lars","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Hans Petter","key":"hougenpau","last":"Hougen","locid":"474ff67a-bdbb-45c6-8350-a838d58936f3","name":"Hougen, Hans Petter","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars F.","key":"rickeltpau","last":"Rickelt","locid":"1219da53-d87c-4aa5-8154-704c783f4590","name":"Rickelt, Lars F","name_org":"Rickelt, Lars F.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael","key":"kühlpau","last":"Kühl","locid":"0335a969-c4b7-413d-981d-e7eedffb49f5","name":"Kühl, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-1792-4790","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels","key":"høibypau","last":"Høiby","locid":"9dab27ed-3b7b-4a40-b944-1c0067e62930","name":"Høiby, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-1347-725X","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"bjarnsholtpau","last":"Bjarnsholt","locid":"cb3ccb7d-0415-40e5-9bba-c9bc26b6316d","name":"Bjarnsholt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-8003-7414","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25114118"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/iai.01969-14","issn":["00199567","10706313"],"issn_org":["00199567"],"issue":"11","journal":"Infection and Immunity","pages":"4477-4486","status":"p","title":"Infection and Immunity","volume":"82"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84907960445"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-24588e80-8d2c-487e-ae55-459b9487ef73"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Polymorphonuclear leukocytes restrict growth of <i>Pseudomonas aeruginosa</i> in the lungs of cystic fibrosis patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-415109","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Umbilical and epigastric hernia repairs are minor, but are commonly conducted surgical procedures. Long-term results have only been sparsely investigated. Our objective was to investigate the risk of chronic complaints after a simple sutured repair for small umbilical and epigastric hernias. METHODS: A retrospective cohort study with a 5-year questionnaire and clinical follow-up was conducted. Patients undergoing primary elective, open non-mesh umbilical or epigastric sutured hernia repair were included. Patients completed a structured questionnaire regarding chronic complaints during work and leisure activities using a verbal rating scale. The primary outcome was chronic complaints. RESULTS: A total of 295 patients were included for analysis after a median of 5.0-year (range 2.8-8.0) follow-up period. Follow-up results were achieved from 262 of the included patients (90 % response rate). Up till 5.8 % of the patients reported moderate or severe pain and discomfort. Work and leisure activities were restricted in 8.5 and 10.0 % of patients, respectively. Patients with chronic complaints had a higher incidence of recurrence (clinical and reoperation), than patients with none or mild complaints (78.6 vs. 22.2 % (P < 0.001)). The recurrence rate was significantly higher after a repair with absorbable suture (20.1 %) compared with non-absorbable suture repair (4.2 %) (P < 0.001). CONCLUSION: We found that chronic complaints after a simple sutured umbilical or epigastric repair was in the level of 5.5 % and could in part be explained by recurrence. Furthermore, absorbable suture should be omitted to reduce risk of recurrence.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Westen, Mikkel","Christoffersen, Mette W","Jørgensen, Lars Nannestad","Stigaard, Trine","Bisgaard, Thue"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518792"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Female","Follow Up Studies","Hernia Abdominal","Hernia Umbilical","Herniorrhaphy","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Postoperative Complications","Questionnaires","Recurrence","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Suture Techniques","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"chronic complaints after simple sutured repair for umbilical or epigastric hernias may be related to recurrence","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00423-013-1119-9","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-518792","identifier":[{"id":"24037253","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84893652546","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d1bfe890-9d42-40a5-948f-49055c05ac93"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Hernia, Abdominal","Hernia, Umbilical","Herniorrhaphy","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Postoperative Complications","Questionnaires","Recurrence","Reoperation","Retrospective Studies","Risk Factors","Suture Techniques","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8B591BC45D0A85AB97D7D29995257C3A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00423-013-1119-9","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person