"scoID":["2-s2.0-84912013464"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-44c479c6-851f-4bc0-aad9-7ae23763cc9d","ku-696f26f6-1277-42e2-8074-c7405b05b793"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Functional network analysis of obese and lean Göttingen minipigs elucidates changes in oxidative and inflammatory networks in obese pigs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.61-034142","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"A dichotomous choice for metazoan cells is between proliferation and differentiation. Measuring tRNA pools in various cell types, we found two distinct subsets, one that is induced in proliferating cells, and repressed otherwise, and another with the opposite signature. Correspondingly, we found that genes serving cell-autonomous functions and genes involved in multicellularity obey distinct codon usage. Proliferation-induced and differentiation-induced tRNAs often carry anticodons that correspond to the codons enriched among the cell-autonomous and the multicellularity genes, respectively. Because mRNAs of cell-autonomous genes are induced in proliferation and cancer in particular, the concomitant induction of their codon-enriched tRNAs suggests coordination between transcription and translation. Histone modifications indeed change similarly in the vicinity of cell-autonomous genes and their corresponding tRNAs, and in multicellularity genes and their tRNAs, suggesting the existence of transcriptional programs coordinating tRNA supply and demand. Hence, we describe the existence of two distinct translation programs that operate during proliferation and differentiation.","author_count":28,"contributors":["Gingold, Hila","Tehler, Disa","Christoffersen, Nanna R","Nielsen, Morten Muhlig","Asmar, Fazila","Kooistra, Susanne M","Christophersen, Nicolaj S","Christensen, Lise Lotte","Borre, Michael","Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard","Dyrskjøt, Lars","Andersen, Claus Lindbjerg","Hulleman, Esther","Wurdinger, Tom","Ralfkiær, Elisabeth","Helin, Kristian","Grønbæk, Kirsten","Ørntoft, Torben Falck","Waszak, Sebastian M","Dahan, Orna","Pedersen, Jakob Skou","Lund, Anders H","Pilpel, Yitzhak"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-020249"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Israel","Netherlands","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Amsterdam UMC","Laboratory of Integrative and Systems Physiology, School of Life Sciences, École Polytechnique Fédérale, 1015 Lausanne, Switzerland.","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam","Weizmann Institute of Science","École Polytechnique Fédérale de Lausanne"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a dual program for translation regulation in cellular proliferation and differentiation","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2014.08.011","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-020249","identifier":[{"id":"25215487","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84908078106","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-683bf426-32e9-4b5a-92c6-9f34c0850810","ku-0628c231-5ea1-4891-a8fe-77099dc0f547"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2705ABCBDB84587AD7C6A2B6A222167B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2014.08.011","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"il","key":"weizmann institute of science","loc":["Israel","Asia, Middle East","OECD"],"name":"Weizmann Institute of Science","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, BRIC, Lund Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l