d496724e","name":"Christoffersen, Kirsten Seestern","orcid":"0000-0002-3324-1017","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Magnus","key":"lundmagnuspau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Magnus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Palle","key":"smedegaardnielsenpallepau","last":"Smedegaard Nielsen","name":"Smedegaard Nielsen, Palle","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin","key":"ulrikchristensenmartinpau","last":"Ulrik Christensen","name":"Ulrik Christensen, Martin","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtnielsmartinpau","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lillian Magelund","key":"jensenlillianmagelundpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Lillian Magelund","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"raschmortenpedh","last":"Rasch","name":"Rasch, Morten","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtnielsmartinpedh","last":"Schmidt","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788771560435"],"pages":"38-63","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","publisher_org":"Aarhus University, DCE – Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","status":"p","subtitle":"18<sup>th</sup> Annual Report 2012","title":"Zackenberg Ecological Research Operations"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ba170f61-211f-4806-82c5-38b5afc77696"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Zackenberg Basic : The BioBasis programme","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-504513","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Apolipoprotein M (apoM) is a plasma apolipoprotein that mainly associates with high-density lipoproteins. Hence, most studies on apoM so far have investigated its effect on and association with lipid metabolism and atherosclerosis. The insight into apoM biology recently took a major turn. ApoM was identified as a carrier of the bioactive lipid sphingosine-1-phosphate (S1P). S1P activates five different G-protein-coupled receptors, known as the S1P-receptors 1-5 and, hence, affects a wide range of biological processes, such as lymphocyte trafficking, angiogenesis, wound repair and even virus suppression and cancer. The ability of apoM to bind S1P is due to a lipophilic binding pocket within the lipocalin structure of the apoM molecule. Mice overexpressing apoM have increased plasma S1P concentrations, whereas apoM-deficient mice have decreased S1P levels. ApoM-S1P is able to activate the S1P-receptor-1, affecting the function of endothelial cells, and apoM-deficient mice display impaired endothelial permeability in the lung. This review will focus on the putative biological roles of the new apoM-S1P axis in relation to lipoprotein metabolism, lipid disorders and atherosclerosis.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Arkensteijn, Bas W C","Berbée, Jimmy F P","Rensen, Patrick C N","Nielsen, Lars Bo","Christoffersen, Christina"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-493243"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the apolipoprotein m sphingosine 000000000001 phosphate axis biological relevance in lipoprotein metabolism lipid disorders and atherosclerosis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms14034419","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-493243","identifier":[{"id":"23439550","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84875080243","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3634416","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a720ffc8-9746-489a-90ab-2984009620ca"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B80FC5B2BDB78D04F805B9401897E90"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijms14034419","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Bas W C","key":"arkensteijnpau","last":"Arkensteijn","locid":"ae2765bf-2deb-4a8d-ae60-906fbc349b45","name":"Arkensteijn, Bas W C","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jimmy F P","key":"berbéepau","last":"Berbée","name":"Berbée, Jimmy F P","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Patrick C N","key":"rensenpau","last":"Rensen","name":"Rensen, Patrick C N","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars B","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","name_org":"Nielsen, Lars B","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23439550"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/ijms14034419","issn":["14220067","16616596"],"issn_org":["16616596"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","pages":"4419-31","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences","title_org":"International Journal of Molecular Sciences (Online)","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84875080243"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a720ffc8-9746-489a-90ab-2984009620ca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The apolipoprotein m-sphingosine-1-phosphate axis : biological relevance in lipoprotein metabolism, lipid disorders and atherosclerosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-493243","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Uraemia is a strong risk factor for cardiovascular disease. Osteopontin (OPN) is highly expressed in aortas of uraemic apolipoprotein E knockout (E KO) mice. OPN affects key atherogenic processes, i.e. inflammation and phenotypic modulation of smooth muscle cells (SMCs). We explored the role of OPN on vascular pathology in uraemic mice.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Tanja Xenia","Madsen, Marie","Nielsen, Nanna Maria Junker","Christoffersen, Christina","Vikeså, Jonas","Bro, Susanne","Hultgårdh-Nilsson, Anna","Nielsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-542261"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"osteopontin deficiency dampens the pro atherogenic effect of uraemia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/cvr/cvt049","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-542261","identifier":[{"id":"23455547","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84877942003","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f95cec69-9d34-4c28-9cad-b9af04325b40"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E02213D34F575B1DDED30AD741FC1FC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/cvr/cvt049","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tanja Xenia","key":"pedersentanjaxeniapau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"78b12e4c-f5b0-433c-adae-ee24837bb372","name":"Pedersen, Tanja Xenia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie","key":"madsenmariepau","last":"Madsen","locid":"2552b6c8-6b3a-41c7-aec6-bb2be67d1bf1","name":"Madsen, Marie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nanna Maria Junker","key":"nielsennannamariajunkerpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"a35e2345-80ff-4554-aad3-92023fa268b8","name":"Nielsen, Nanna Maria Junker","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenchristinapau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"vikesåjonaspau","last":"Vikeså","locid":"74dd4b6b-36f4-4fb4-8479-698b7c533e25","name":"Vikeså, Jonas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susanne","key":"brosusannepau","last":"Bro","locid":"c84951f6-d903-4390-93a9-eede07e2a005","name":"Bro, Susanne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"hultgårdhnilssonannapau","last":"Hultgårdh-Nilsson","name":"Hultgårdh-Nilsson, Anna","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenlarsbopau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23455547"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/cvr/cvt049","issn":["00086363","17553245"],"issn_org":["00086363"],"issue":"3","journal":"Cardiovascular Research","pages":"352-9","status":"p","title":"Cardiovascular Research","volume":"98"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84877942003"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f95cec69-9d34-4c28-9cad-b9af04325b40"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Osteopontin deficiency dampens the pro-atherogenic effect of uraemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-542261","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Lack of animal models with human-like size and pathology hampers translational research in atherosclerosis. Mouse models are missing central features of human atherosclerosis and are too small for intravascular procedures and imaging. Modeling the disease in minipigs may overcome these limitations, but it has proven difficult to induce rapid atherosclerosis in normal pigs by high-fat feeding alone, and genetically modified models similar to those created in mice are not available. D374Y gain-of-function mutations in the proprotein convertase subtilisin/kexin type 9 (PCSK9) gene cause severe autosomal dominant hypercholesterolemia and accelerates atherosclerosis in humans. Using Sleeping Beauty DNA transposition and cloning by somatic cell nuclear transfer, we created Yucatan minipigs with liver-specific expression of human D374Y-PCSK9. D374Y-PCSK9 transgenic pigs displayed reduced hepatic low-density lipoprotein (LDL) receptor levels, impaired LDL clearance, severe hypercholesterolemia, and spontaneous development of progressive atherosclerotic lesions that could be visualized by noninvasive imaging. This model should prove useful for several types of translational research in atherosclerosis.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Al-Mashhadi, Rozh","Sørensen, Charlotte Brandt","Kragh, Peter M","Christoffersen, Christina","Mortensen, Martin Bødtker","Tolbod, Lars Poulsen","Thim, Troels","Du, Yutao","Li, Juan","Liu, Ying","Moldt, Brian","Schmidt, Mette","Vajta, Gabor","Larsen, Torben","Purup, Stig","Bolund, Lars","Nielsen, Lars B","Callesen, Henrik","Falk, Erling","Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm","Bentzon, Jacob Fog"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016031"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Animals","Animals Genetically Modified","Atherosclerosis","Cloning Organism","DNA","Disease Models Animal","Female","Humans","Hypercholesterolemia","Hyperlipoproteinemia Type II","Liver",