{"abstract":"The HDL associated apolipoprotein M (apoM) protects against experimental atherosclerosis but the mechanism is unknown. ApoM increases prebeta-HDL formation. We explored whether plasma apoM affects mobilization of cholesterol from peripheral cells in mice.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Elsøe, Sara","Christoffersen, Christina","Luchoomun, Jayraz","Turner, Scott","Nielsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-462179"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Apolipoproteins","Atherosclerosis","Bile","Cell Line","Cholesterol","Feces","Foam Cells","Gene Deletion","Humans","Lipid Metabolism","Lipoproteins HDL","Macrophages","Mice","Mice Inbred C57BL","Mice Transgenic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"apolipoprotein m promotes mobilization of cellular cholesterol in vivo","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbalip.2013.04.009","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-462179","identifier":[{"id":"84878422212","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24046869","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-7303eb6e-0b4a-4c68-b36d-9e6ee915d556"],"keyword":["Animals","Apolipoproteins","Atherosclerosis","Bile","Cell Line","Cholesterol","Feces","Foam Cells","Gene Deletion","Humans","Lipid Metabolism","Lipoproteins, HDL","Macrophages","Mice","Mice, Inbred C57BL","Mice, Transgenic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9AFD6FCCB7D4AB00FF60EFEAC8956E51"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bbalip.2013.04.009","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sara","key":"elsøepau","last":"Elsøe","name":"Elsøe, Sara","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jayraz","key":"luchoomunpau","last":"Luchoomun","name":"Luchoomun, Jayraz","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Scott","key":"turnerpau","last":"Turner","name":"Turner, Scott","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24046869"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbalip.2013.04.009","issn":["13881981","18792618"],"issn_org":["13881981"],"issue":"7","journal":"BBA - Molecular and Cell Biology of Lipids","pages":"1287-92","status":"p","title":"BBA - Molecular and Cell Biology of Lipids","title_org":"Biochimica et Biophysica Acta - Molecular and Cell Biology of Lipids","volume":"1831"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878422212"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7303eb6e-0b4a-4c68-b36d-9e6ee915d556"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Apolipoprotein M promotes mobilization of cellular cholesterol in vivo","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-462179","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Purpose of review: The review will address the potential roles of apolipoprotein M (apoM) as a carrier protein and modulator of sphingosine-1-phosphate (S1P) bioactivity. Recent findings: Recombinant apoM can bind small lipids such as retinoic acid, oxidized phospholipids, and S1P. Thus, the effects of apoM may be pleiotrophic. The S1P binding ability of apoM has biological impact. ApoM-bound S1P can activate S1P1 receptors on endothelial cells and deficiency of apoM abolishes the presence of S1P in HDL. In mice, the lack of apoM causes dysfunctional endothelial barrier function in the lungs. In humans, sepsis that is characterized by impaired endothelial function is associated with low plasma apoM. Summary: Plasma apoM is mainly bound to HDL. The roles of apoM in atherosclerosis and lipoprotein metabolism have been given much attention. New in the field is the discovery of apoM as a chaperone for S1P. S1P is a bioactive lipid with effects on angiogenesis, lymphocyte trafficking, endothelial cell migration, and inflammation. A drug targeting the S1P-system (fingolimod) is now used for treatment of multiple sclerosis. It improves the blood–brain barrier and inhibits migration of lymphocytes into the brain. Further exploration of the apoM/S1P axis may uncover its potential as a biomarker and target for new treatments.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Christina","Nielsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-503962"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Animals","Apolipoproteins","Atherosclerosis","Endothelial Cells","Humans","Lipid Metabolism","Lipocalins","Lipoproteins HDL","Lysophospholipids","Protein Binding","Sepsis","Sphingosine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"apolipoprotein m bridging hdl and endothelial function","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/MOL.0b013e328361f6ad","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-503962","identifier":[{"id":"84880595495","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23652568","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b925e39e-0dbb-4616-98ba-c44763bc3534"],"keyword":["Animals","Apolipoproteins","Atherosclerosis","Endothelial Cells","Humans","Lipid Metabolism","Lipocalins","Lipoproteins, HDL","Lysophospholipids","Protein Binding","Sepsis","Sphingosine"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E724C3D3BB6BCC67B8CB177B928F46E2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/MOL.0b013e328361f6ad","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Physiology of circulation, kidney and lung"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23652568"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/mol.0b013e328361f6ad","issn":["09579672","1080823X"],"issn_org":["09579672"],"issue":"4","journal":"Current Opinion in Lipidology","pages":"295-300","status":"p","title":"Current Opinion in Lipidology","volume":"24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84880595495"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b925e39e-0dbb-4616-98ba-c44763bc3534"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Apolipoprotein M : bridging HDL and endothelial function","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-503962","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Giselle","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","Petrini, Laura"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-087733"],"event":{"end":"2012-07-27","place":"Cape Town, za","start":"2012-07-22","title":"International Congress of Psychology","year":"2012"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"mirror illusions understanding individual differences","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.icp2012.com/IJP%20Supplement%20Abstracts.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-087733","identifier":[{"id":"84859180769","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-819ac155-0b9b-46e3-87c5-3a51cdac0fd7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3B6F482DF24CFA7B9F340D8F14F48905"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.icp2012.com/IJP%20Supplement%20Abstracts.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology, Center for Sensory-Motor Interaction","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Center for Developmental & Applied Psychological Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Communication and Psychology, Centre for Cognitive Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Giselle","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"3184e478-39eb-431e-8f95-b5a2363c456d","name":"Christoffersen, Giselle","orcid":"0000-0003-1092-7486","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"arendtnielsenpau","last":"Arendt-Nielsen","locid":"1794f9ec-22f1-47af-96c1-88c23c3b06a2","name":"Arendt-Nielsen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0003-0892-1579","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura","key":"petrinipau","last":"Petrini","locid":"667850ce-df5e-433d-9052-a3eb4eee7498","name":"Petrini, Laura","orcid":"0000-0002-5320-1944","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00207594","1464066X"],"issn_org":["00207594"],"journal":"International Journal of Psychology","pages":"111-112","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Psychology","volume":"47"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-819ac155-0b9b-46e3-87c5-3a51cdac0fd7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Mirror illusions : Understanding individual differences","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-087733","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
{"abstract":"Apolipoprotein (apo) M is mainly associated with HDL. Nevertheless, we have consistently observed positive correlations of apoM with plasma LDL cholesterol in humans. Moreover, LDL-receptor deficiency is associated with increased plasma apoM in mice. Here, we tested the idea that plasma apoM concentrations are affected by the rate of LDL-receptor mediated clearance of apoB-containing particles. We measured apoM in humans each carrying one of 3 different LDL-receptor mutations (n=9) or the apoB3500 mutation (n=12). These carriers had increased plasma apoM (1.34±0.13 µmol/L, P=0.003, and 1.23±0.10 µmol/l, P=0.02, respectively) as compared with non-carriers (0.93±0.04 µmol/L). When we injected human apoM-containing HDL into Wt (n=6) or LDL-receptor deficient mice (n=6), the removal of HDL-associated human apoM was delayed in the LDL-receptor deficient mice. After 2 hrs 54±5% versus 90±8% (P <0.005) of the initial amounts of human apoM remained in plasma of Wt and LDL-receptor deficient mice, respectively. Finally, we compared the turnover of radio-iodinated LDL and plasma apoM concentrations in 45 normocholesterolemic humans. There was a negative correlation between plasma apoM and the fractional catabolic rate of LDL (r=-0.38, P=0.009). These data suggest that the plasma clearance of apoM, despite apoM primarily being associated with HDL, is influenced by LDL-receptor mediated clearance of apoB-containing particles.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Christoffersen, Christina","Benn, Marianne","Christensen, Pernille Meyer","Gordts, Philip L S M","Roebroek, Anton J M","Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","Dahlback, Bjorn","Nielsen, Lars Bo"],"cuid":["S02-092.57-045881"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the plasma concentration of hdl associated apolipoprotein m is influenced by ldl receptor mediated clearance of apob containing particles","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1194/jlr.P023697","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.57-045881","identifier":[{"id":"84866178749","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3435552","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"22826357","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c0587edb-3c26-407a-93b6-e4301a0a1254","ku-c674e3fe-caed-4be9-9d52-fa8a0b7ca460"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A93F19598D9F3E88ABD09D740303B7F7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1194/jlr.P023697","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"christoffersenpau","last":"Christoffersen","locid":"7f6ac9b3-a8ee-401d-8c45-dc0bf731314a","name":"Christoffersen, Christina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marianne","key":"bennpau","last":"Benn","locid":"b9e8f763-a852-4910-8b80-6d3b75b4aee3","name":"Benn, Marianne","orcid":"0000-0002-1701-595X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Pernille Møller","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"2a1d9e57-75ed-4b17-bb4a-dc4b68d06f8d","name":"Christensen, Pernille Meyer","name_org":"Christensen, Pernille Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Philip L S M","key":"gordtspau","last":"Gordts","name":"Gordts, Philip L S M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anton J M","key":"roebroekpau","last":"Roebroek","name":"Roebroek, Anton J M","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ruth","key":"frikkeschmidtpau","last":"Frikke-Schmidt","locid":"bce2c3b4-6e08-46c7-96c6-7e385b0ec8b3","name":"Frikke-Schmidt, Ruth","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne","key":"tybjaerghansenpau","last":"Tybjaerg-Hansen","locid":"452a492e-c869-41e5-b60e-1d2a542287cf","name":"Tybjærg-Hansen, Anne","name_org":"Tybjaerg-Hansen, Anne","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bjorn","key":"dahlbackpau","last":"Dahlback","name":"Dahlback, Bjorn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Björn","key":"dahlbäckpau","last":"Dahlbäck","name":"Dahlbäck, Björn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Bo","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"313d9ac1-283c-452d-af72-ab35e031b7aa","name":"Nielsen, Lars Bo","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["22826357"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1194/jlr.p023697","issn":["00222275","15397262"],"issn_org":["00222275"],"issue":"10","journal":"Journal of Lipid Research","pages":"2198-204","status":"p","title":"Journal of Lipid Research","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84866178749"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c0587edb-3c26-407a-93b6-e4301a0a1254","ku-c674e3fe-caed-4be9-9d52-fa8a0b7ca460"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The plasma concentration of HDL-associated apolipoprotein M is influenced by LDL-receptor-mediated clearance of apoB-containing particles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.57-045881","year":"2012","yearsub":"2012"}
